            {
              "type": "Progress Notes",
              "title": "Office Visit",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2023-01-18T16:15",
              "body": "Subjective: About 6 weeks out from a vaginal delivery on 12/9 (induced at 37 wks for the baby's gastroschisis, summary in chart). Saw OB for the postpartum check last week, told she is healing fine. Baby had the repair in the NICU. She is tired, sleep broken, but says mood is ok and she is coping. Some worry but less than in the fall. Back on her usual routine with iron, prenatal and metformin. Planning to go back to work next month.\n\nObjective: Vitals reviewed. Looks tired but bright. Lungs clear, heart regular. Abdomen soft. No calf tenderness.\nPHQ-9 5, GAD-7 7.\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n1. Postpartum, mood screen reassuring. Reviewed warning signs of postpartum depression; she knows to message.\n2. Iron deficiency anemia - CBC and iron studies today, continue ferrous sulfate.\n3. PCOS - continue metformin.\n4. GAD - stable.\nPhysical in June."
            }
          ]
