              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2023-06-14T09:05",
              "body": "29F for her yearly physical. Six months postpartum and back at the store full time. Feels like herself again. Periods have not returned in a regular pattern yet, which is typical for her with PCOS. Anxiety calmer, sleeping better now the baby sleeps longer stretches. Takes metformin, iron, prenatal.\n\nROS otherwise negative.\nMeds/allergies reviewed. Latex, sulfa.\n\nExam: Vitals reviewed. NAD. HEENT normal. Thyroid not enlarged. Lungs clear. RRR, no murmur. Abdomen soft, nontender, well-healed laparoscopy scars. Pelvic: normal external genitalia, cervix without lesion, Pap collected. Extremities without edema. Skin without notable lesions. Mood bright.\nPHQ-9 2, GAD-7 5.\n\nA/P:\n1. Health maintenance - Pap today (last 2020, normal). Fasting labs drawn. Hep C/HIV already done 2022. Flu shot in the fall.\n2. PCOS - metformin, A1c today.\n3. Iron deficiency anemia - recheck CBC and iron.\n4. GAD - mild, stable.\nReturn in about 6 months."
            }
