              "body": "Physical, age 30. Store was short-staffed this spring and she has been covering extra shifts; more worry and trouble switching off at night. No panic episodes. Not interested in changing anything right now, wants to see if it eases as staffing improves. Kids keep her busy.\nMeds: metformin 500 bid, ferrous sulfate, prenatal. Allergies latex, sulfa.\n\nExam: vitals reviewed. Well appearing. Thyroid normal. Lungs clear, heart regular. Abdomen benign. No edema.\nPHQ-9 4, GAD-7 9.\n\nA/P\n1. GAD - score up a few points with work stress. Discussed sleep routine and protected time off. Recheck in 6 months, sooner if needed.\n2. PCOS - stable on metformin. A1c, lipids today.\n3. Iron deficiency anemia - CBC, iron studies.\n4. HM - Pap current (2023). Flu vaccine this fall."
